<h2 style="font-size:27px;line-height:1.5">9. How to Make Your First Trade on OKX</h2>

<p>If your account already has USDT, new users can start with <strong>Spot trading</strong> to learn the trading interface.</p>

<p>For example, to buy BTC with USDT:</p>

<p><strong>OKX App → Trade → Spot → Search BTC/USDT → Buy BTC</strong></p>

<p>Then choose an order type.</p>

<h3 style="font-size:23px;line-height:1.6">Market Order</h3>

<p>A market order attempts to execute as quickly as possible using prices currently available in the market.</p>

<p>It is suitable when fast execution is the priority, but you should understand:</p>

<p><strong>Market orders can experience slippage.</strong></p>

<p>Especially when liquidity is lower or the market is moving quickly, the final average fill price may differ from the price you saw when submitting the order.</p>

<h3 style="font-size:23px;line-height:1.6">Limit Order</h3>

<p>A limit order allows you to set the price at which you are willing to buy BTC.</p>

<p>For example, if BTC is currently at 80,000 USDT but you only want to buy at 78,000 USDT, you can place a limit buy order at 78,000 USDT.</p>

<p>The advantage is greater control over the execution price. The disadvantage is:</p>

<p><strong>If the market never reaches your selected price, the order may remain unfilled.</strong></p>

<p>For your first trade, consider using a smaller amount to become familiar with placing orders, canceling orders, checking order history and monitoring asset changes.</p>

